{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And that you went astray.</b> It does not say if you went astray, but rather כי שטית — meaning, a great act of wantonness was in you, and you are worthy of punishment, and this is the disgrace: for you went astray — who has a husband, and despite all this, you hid yourself." "<b>And if you were defiled.</b> And if you were defiled, you shall be flogged, and if not, you shall not be flogged." "<b>Aside from your husband.</b> For the husband's lying with her preceded the paramour's lying with her, and not that the paramour's lying preceded the husband's. Therefore they do not administer the water to arusot (betrothed women)."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:36.505559474Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}